- namespace_command
- grove_template

' What a world can ask for, read off what it holds. Nothing here is stored
' and nothing is registered: every answer is derived from records, the
' references in them, and the reverse index.
'
' Three things are kept apart.
'   declared   a template some world placed where this one can read it. Its
'              record may say what an answer is an instance of (gives) and
'              what each input must be an instance of (takes/<name>). Both
'              are ordinary references to other templates.
'   observed   records that cite a template: instances, and what peers say.
'   reachable  computed from the two and from which peers this world knows.
+ reach
  + gives
    ^ path
    ['gives]
  + takes
    ^ path
    ['takes]
  + offer
    ' A declared template: who placed it, its name and version in that
    ' world's spelling, what it gives and what it takes.
    : by=iota at=safe gives=maybe[safe] takes=row[[slot=path cited=safe]]
  + need
    ' One thing on the way to what is wanted: the template it must be an
    ' instance of, how it stands, and the offer that gives it.
    : want=path status=iota by=maybe[reach/offer]
  + stated
    ' The version a peer published a name at, from the mount's version header.
    \ name=path state=namespace
    ^ nat
    = local=path state.local_name(name)
    ?> (./known records) (namespace/page .x .none local state) 0
    ?> (./some held) records.fil 0
    | held.aeon.oath.version
  + read
    \ name=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ reach/offer
    = version
        ? (reference_index/segment_is name.at(0) state.self) state.case(.x name).fall(0)
        | reach/stated name state
      nothing=maybe[safe] .none
      gives=maybe[safe]
        ?> (./some held) record.get(reach/gives) nothing
        ?> link=safe held nothing
        | ./some link
      none=row[[slot=path cited=safe]] []
      takes
        | record.tap.fold none
          \ out entry
          ? !(pith_prefix reach/takes entry.key) out
          ?> link=safe entry.val out
          | out.snoc([entry.key link])
    | reach/offer name.at(0) (safe version .x name) gives takes
  + within
    \ root=path state=namespace out=row[reach/offer]
    ^ row[reach/offer]
    | (sovereign_peek root state).tap.fold out
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(maybe/is_some record.get(grove_templates/slot)) acc
      = name=path (reference_index/canonical state.self root.weld(rel))
      | acc.snoc((reach/read name record state))
  + offers
    ' Declared: every template in what this world publishes and in what its
    ' peers published to it.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ row[reach/offer]
    = none=row[reach/offer] []
      mine (reach/within [state.self 'our] state none)
    | reach/within [state.self 'her] state mine
  + cited
    ' Observed: the records citing a name, each in its own world's spelling,
    ' with the slot the reference sits in.
    \ target=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[holder=path slot=path]]
    = none=row[[holder=path slot=path]] []
      reader (sovereign_reader state)
      name=path (reader.canonical target)
    ?> (./known edges) (reader.edges 0 name) none
    | edges.fold none
      \ out=row[[holder=path slot=path]] edge=reference_edge
      ^ row[[holder=path slot=path]]
      ? !(equal[path] edge.target.path name) out
      | out.snoc([edge.holder edge.slot])
  + held
    ' An instance of a template that another world made for this one: its
    ' name in that world's spelling.
    \ template=path state=namespace
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    | (reach/cited template state).fold none
      \ acc [holder slot]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(equal[path] slot grove_templates/source_slot) acc
      ? !(maybe/is_some (reference_index/mounted state.self holder)) acc
      | ./some holder
  + witnesses
    ' Observed: the worlds, other than this one and the template's own, whose
    ' records published to this one cite a template.
    \ template=path state=namespace
    ^ row[iota]
    = none=row[iota] []
    ? (eq template.len 0) none
    | (reach/cited template state).fold none
      \ acc [holder slot]
      ? (eq holder.len 0) acc
      = world holder.at(0)
      ? (reference_index/segment_is world state.self) acc
      ? (reference_index/segment_is world template.at(0)) acc
      ? (acc.any((\ seen=iota (reference_index/segment_is seen world)))) acc
      | acc.snoc(world)
  + giver
    ' The declared offer whose answers are instances of a template.
    \ wanted=path known=row[reach/offer]
    ^ maybe[reach/offer]
    = none=maybe[reach/offer] .none
    | known.fold none
      \ acc=maybe[reach/offer] item=reach/offer
      ^ maybe[reach/offer]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ?> (./some link) item.gives acc
      ? !(equal[path] link.path wanted) acc
      | ./some item
  + knows
    ' Whether this world keeps anything on a card for a world.
    \ world=iota state=namespace
    ^ bool
    | gt (sovereign_peek [state.self 'io 'mesa world] state).wyt 0
  + walk
    \ wanted=path depth=nat seen=row[reach/need] known=row[reach/offer] state=namespace
    ^ row[reach/need]
    = nobody=maybe[reach/offer] .none
      here=iota 'held
      lost=iota 'unknown
      deep=iota 'deep
      near=iota 'ask
      far=iota 'stranger
    ? (seen.any((\ item=reach/need (equal[path] item.want wanted)))) seen
    ? (maybe/is_some (reach/held wanted state)) seen.snoc((reach/need wanted here nobody))
    ?> (./some via) (reach/giver wanted known) seen.snoc((reach/need wanted lost nobody))
    ? (eq depth 0) seen.snoc((reach/need wanted deep nobody))
    = below
        | via.takes.fold seen
          \ acc [slot cited]
          | reach/walk cited.path depth.dec acc known state
      status (? (reach/knows via.by state) near far)
    | below.snoc((reach/need wanted status (./some via)))
  + way
    ' Reachable: everything needed before an instance of a template can be
    ' asked for, inputs before what takes them, each with how it stands:
    '   held      an instance made for this world is already here
    '   ask       an offer gives it, placed by a world this one knows
    '   stranger  an offer gives it, placed by a world this one has no card for
    '   unknown   nothing this world can read says how it is given
    ' What an offerer will in fact answer stays its own decision.
    \ wanted=path state=namespace
    ^ row[reach/need]
    = none=row[reach/need] []
    | reach/walk wanted 8 none (reach/offers state) state
